```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In @.agents/plugins/opencode-aidevops/config-hook.mjs around lines 20 - 29, The
upsert currently skips updating existing anthropic models based solely on
matching name, which leaves stale attachment/modalities values; in the upsert
flow that consumes claudeModelDef(overrides) remove or modify the name-only
guard so the update merges these default fields into existing records (ensure
attachment, tool_call, temperature, reasoning, modalities, cost are
overwritten/merged from claudeModelDef rather than skipped). Locate the upsert
logic that checks the model name (the guard around the upsert for
anthropic/Claude entries) and change it to either compare and patch differences
or always apply the claudeModelDef defaults when provider/type matches, so
existing entries get the new image/attachment defaults. Ensure the code merges
overrides from claudeModelDef(overrides) into the existing record rather than
returning early.
