body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

`evictStaleConversations` only removes entries from `conversationStates`. However, `activeBridges` can also contain lingering bridge handles (and their associated child processes and timers) for conversations that are no longer active. If a conversation is evicted due to inactivity, its corresponding entry in `activeBridges` should also be cleaned up to prevent resource leaks (lingering child processes).

```javascript
function evictStaleConversations() {
  const now = Date.now();
  for (const [key, stored] of conversationStates) {
    if (now - stored.lastAccessMs > CONVERSATION_TTL_MS) {
      conversationStates.delete(key);
      const active = activeBridges.get(key);
      if (active) {
        clearInterval(active.heartbeatTimer);
        active.bridge.end();
        activeBridges.delete(key);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

